---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How F1Visa.Net collects, uses, and protects your personal information — including identity verification (KYC), payments, and AI-assisted guidance. Operated by Web3 Freedom Club DAO LLC."
>
	<LegalPage
		eyebrow="Privacy Policy"
		title="Your privacy, on the record."
		lead="F1Visa.Net is a member-owned cooperative built on trust. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect when you use f1visa.net, how we use it, who we share it with, and the choices you have over your data."
		updated="September 2, 2026"
	>
		<h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
		<p>
			F1Visa.Net ("F1Visa.Net," "we," "us," or "our") is an AI-powered platform
			that helps F-1 visa holders and applicants navigate the U.S. student visa
			journey through AI-assisted guidance, community, mentorship, and
			educational resources. The site is operated by{" "}
			<strong>Web3 Freedom Club DAO LLC</strong>, a Colorado limited liability
			company based in the United States. This Privacy Policy applies to your
			use of f1visa.net and the services we provide through it.
		</p>
		<p>
			This policy describes our practices in connection with information we
			collect through the website, forms, accounts, AI assistant, and related
			services (collectively, the "Service"). By using the Service, you agree
			to the practices described in this policy.
		</p>

		<h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
		<p>We collect information you give us, information collected automatically, and information from certain third parties. The categories are described below.</p>

		<h3>2.1 Information You Provide Directly</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Account and waitlist registration:</strong> name, email
				address, country, visa status/stage, and any other details you enter
				when you join the waitlist or create an account.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Contact inquiries:</strong> name, email address, university
				(optional), and the content of your message when you contact us
				through the contact form.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Community participation:</strong> profile information, forum
				posts, comments, and messages you contribute to the community.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Assessment and survey responses:</strong> answers you provide
				to the AI Readiness Assessment or other questionnaires, including
				results derived from those answers.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>AI assistant conversations:</strong> the prompts, questions,
				and visa-related information you share with our AI assistant
				(WeOwnChat, powered by the Hermes AI agent), along with the responses
				generated for you.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Payment information:</strong> when you purchase a membership
				tier or become a member-owner, payment details (such as name, billing
				address, and card data) are collected and processed by our payment
				processor, <strong>Stripe</strong>. We do not store full payment card
				numbers on our own systems.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h3>2.2 Identity Verification (KYC) Data</h3>
		<div class="legal-notice">
			<p>
				<strong>KYC identity verification:</strong> To become a cooperative
				member-owner, we may require identity verification ("Know Your
				Customer" or KYC) through our verification provider,{" "}
				<strong>Persona</strong>. If and when KYC verification is required,
				Persona may collect your name, date of birth, government-issued ID
				(such as a passport), address, and a facial image or selfie for
				liveness checks. This information is collected and processed by
				Persona on our behalf under its own privacy and security practices.
				We receive only the verification result (e.g., verified or
				not-verified) and the minimal identity details needed to issue your
				membership, unless the verification workflow requires otherwise. KYC
				verification is a planned compliance step and is currently in
				development; it will apply only when we introduce it for
				membership.
			</p>
		</div>

		<h3>2.3 Information Collected Automatically</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Usage and analytics data:</strong> we use{" "}
				<strong>PostHog</strong> to understand how visitors use the Service.
				This includes pages visited, clicks and interactions, referral
				sources, device and browser information, operating system, language
				preferences, approximate location derived from IP address, and error
				reports (including automatic exception capture).
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Cookies and similar technologies:</strong> we and our
				service providers use cookies, localStorage, and similar technologies
				to remember your preferences (such as light/dark theme), authenticate
				sessions, and support analytics. See Section 6 for details.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Log and security data:</strong> our hosting provider
				(Cloudflare) and our infrastructure generate server logs that may
				include IP addresses, request timestamps, and user-agent strings for
				security and reliability purposes.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
		<p>We use the information we collect for the following purposes:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>To provide the Service:</strong> operate your account,
				deliver AI-assisted guidance and answers, maintain the community
				forum, and provide the resources and tools you request.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>To process payments and memberships:</strong> complete
				transactions, manage subscriptions, issue membership certificates,
				and administer cooperative member benefits.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>To verify identity (KYC):</strong> confirm eligibility and
				identity for cooperative membership through Persona, prevent fraud,
				and meet applicable legal and compliance obligations.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>To communicate with you:</strong> respond to inquiries, send
				service notices, and — with your consent or where permitted by law —
				newsletters, visa tips, and updates about the Service.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>To improve the Service:</strong> analyze usage patterns,
				measure feature performance, and improve our AI assistant and
				community experience.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>To ensure safety and security:</strong> detect, prevent, and
				respond to fraud, abuse, security incidents, and violations of our
				Terms of Service.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>To comply with law:</strong> satisfy legal obligations,
				resolve disputes, and enforce our agreements.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Where the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) or comparable law
			applies, our legal bases for processing include performing our contract
			with you, your consent (which you may withdraw at any time), our
			legitimate interests in operating and improving the Service, and
			compliance with legal obligations.
		</p>

		<h2>4. How We Share Your Information</h2>
		<p>
			We do not sell your personal information. We do not rent, trade, or
			share your personal information for third-party advertising. We share
			information only with service providers that help us operate the
			Service, or as required by law:
		</p>
		<table>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th>Service Provider</th>
					<th>What They Process</th>
					<th>Why</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr>
					<td><strong>Stripe</strong></td>
					<td>Payment details, billing information, transaction records</td>
					<td>Subscription and one-time payment processing, fraud prevention</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td><strong>Persona</strong></td>
					<td>Government ID, date of birth, name, address, facial image (liveness)</td>
					<td>KYC identity verification for cooperative membership</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td><strong>Hermes AI agent / WeOwnChat</strong></td>
					<td>Prompts, questions, and conversation content you submit to the AI assistant</td>
					<td>Generating AI-assisted immigration guidance and answers</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td><strong>PostHog</strong></td>
					<td>Usage events, pageviews, device data, anonymized identifiers</td>
					<td>Product analytics and service improvement</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td><strong>Cloudflare</strong></td>
					<td>Request logs, IP addresses, serving infrastructure</td>
					<td>Hosting, CDN delivery, DDoS protection, reliability</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td><strong>Community platform</strong></td>
					<td>Profile data, forum posts, messages</td>
					<td>Hosting the community forum (FluentCommunity on WordPress)</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p>
			We may also disclose information (a) to comply with a court order,
			subpoena, or other legal process; (b) to enforce our Terms of Service;
			(c) to protect the rights, property, or safety of F1Visa.Net, our
			members, or the public; or (d) in connection with a merger, acquisition,
			reorganization, or transfer of all or substantially all of our assets.
		</p>

		<h2>5. AI Processing</h2>
		<p>
			Our AI assistant (WeOwnChat, powered by the Hermes AI agent) processes
			the questions and information you submit to generate guidance. AI
			assistance is provided for educational purposes and does not constitute
			legal advice. You should not submit sensitive personal data (such as
			passport numbers or financial account details) to the AI assistant. See
			our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> for the full AI disclaimer.
		</p>

		<h2>6. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
		<p>We use the following categories of cookies and similar technologies:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Strictly necessary:</strong> required for the Service to
				function, including session cookies and our theme preference cookie.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Analytics:</strong> PostHog sets cookies and uses localStorage
				to record usage events, pageviews, and interaction data so we can
				improve the Service.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Payment and verification:</strong> Stripe and Persona may set
				cookies or embed scripts when you initiate a checkout or verification
				flow.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			You can control cookies through your browser settings or by opting out
			of analytics as described in Section 8. Consult each provider's cookie
			policy for more detail.
		</p>

		<h2>7. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Account and profile data:</strong> retained for as long as
				your account is active, plus a reasonable period afterward to comply
				with legal obligations (for example, tax and record-keeping
				requirements) and to resolve disputes.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Payment records:</strong> retained as required by applicable
				financial and tax law (typically at least several years), while card
				data itself remains with Stripe under its retention practices.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>KYC verification data:</strong> retained only as long as
				needed for the verification purpose, compliance, and fraud prevention,
				and in accordance with Persona's practices and applicable law.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Analytics data:</strong> aggregated and retained for the
				periods required by our analytics provider (typically up to 12–24
				months), after which it is archived or deleted.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>AI conversation data:</strong> retained to improve the
				assistant and for support; you may request deletion as described
				below.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			You may request deletion of your personal information at any time. We
			will delete or anonymize your information unless we are required by law
			to retain it. Contact us at{" "}
			<a href="mailto:support@f1visa.net">support@f1visa.net</a> to make a
			request (see Section 8 for your full rights).
		</p>

		<h2>8. Your Rights and Choices</h2>

		<h3>8.1 California (CCPA/CPRA) and Colorado Residents</h3>
		<p>
			If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act
			(CCPA) and the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA) give you the
			following rights, subject to certain limitations:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Know and access:</strong> request the categories and specific
				pieces of personal information we have collected about you.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Delete:</strong> request deletion of your personal
				information, subject to legal exceptions.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Correct:</strong> request correction of inaccurate personal
				information we hold about you.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Opt out of sale or sharing:</strong> we do not sell or share
				your personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising,
				so we do not currently offer a separate opt-out — but you may always
				contact us with questions.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Limit sensitive data use:</strong> we only use sensitive
				personal information (such as KYC identity data) for the purpose you
				provided it.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Non-discrimination:</strong> we will not discriminate against
				you for exercising any of these rights.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			If you are a Colorado resident, the Colorado Privacy Act provides
			similar rights, including the right to opt out of processing for
			targeted advertising and profiling. We do not engage in those practices
			today.
		</p>

		<h3>8.2 EEA, UK, and Other Regions</h3>
		<p>
			If you are located in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or
			another region with comparable privacy law, you may have the right to
			access, rectify, erase, restrict, port, and object to the processing of
			your personal information, and to withdraw consent at any time. To
			exercise these rights, contact us using the details in Section 11.
		</p>

		<h3>8.3 Analytics and Marketing Choices</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Analytics opt-out:</strong> you can opt out of PostHog
				tracking by using PostHog's opt-out preference or by blocking
				analytics scripts in your browser (for example, with an ad/tracker
				blocker). If you opt out, we may still collect limited, necessary
				log data for security.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Email communications:</strong> you can unsubscribe from
				marketing emails at any time using the link in any email we send.
				Transactional emails (e.g., payment receipts, security notices) may
				continue after you opt out of marketing.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Global Privacy Control (GPC):</strong> we honor Global
				Privacy Control signals where the law requires us to do so.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h3>8.4 How to Exercise Your Rights</h3>
		<p>
			To exercise any of these rights, email{" "}
			<a href="mailto:support@f1visa.net">support@f1visa.net</a> with the
			subject "Privacy Request." We will verify your identity before acting on
			your request to protect your information. We aim to respond within the
			timeframe required by applicable law, typically within 30–45 days, and
			will notify you if we need more time. You may also designate an
			authorized agent to make a request on your behalf.
		</p>

		<h2>9. International Data Transfers</h2>
		<p>
			F1Visa.Net is operated in the United States, and the Service uses
			Cloudflare's global edge network. If you access the Service from outside
			the United States, your information may be processed and stored in the
			United States and other countries where our service providers operate.
			Where required, we rely on appropriate safeguards (such as standard
			contractual clauses) for transfers of personal information. By using
			the Service, you understand that your information may be transferred to
			and processed in the United States.
		</p>

		<h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			The Service is intended for individuals who are at least 18 years old,
			and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children
			under the age of 16. If you believe a child has provided us with
			personal information, please contact us and we will delete it.
		</p>

		<h2>11. Data Security</h2>
		<p>
			We take reasonable and appropriate technical and organizational
			measures to protect your information, including encryption in transit
			(TLS), access controls, and security hardening (including the
			Minimus.io hardening framework used on our AI infrastructure). No
			method of transmission or storage is 100% secure, and we cannot
			guarantee absolute security. You are responsible for keeping your
			account credentials confidential and for not submitting sensitive
			personal data (such as passport numbers or full financial account
			details) to the AI assistant or public community areas.
		</p>

		<h2>12. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
		<p>
			We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make
			material changes, we will post the updated policy on this page and
			update the "Last updated" date. If a change is significant, we will
			make reasonable efforts to notify you (for example, by email or an
			in-Service notice). Your continued use of the Service after changes
			become effective constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
		</p>

		<h2>13. Contact Us</h2>
		<p>
			If you have questions, concerns, or complaints about this Privacy
			Policy or our privacy practices, or if you wish to exercise your rights,
			please contact us:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Company:</strong> Web3 Freedom Club DAO LLC
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Email:</strong>{" "}
				<a href="mailto:support@f1visa.net">support@f1visa.net</a> (privacy
				inquiries) · <a href="mailto:hello@f1visa.net">hello@f1visa.net</a>
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://f1visa.net">f1visa.net</a>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			If we are unable to resolve your concern, you may have the right to
			file a complaint with the data protection authority or state attorney
			general in your jurisdiction.
		</p>
	</LegalPage>
</Base>
